    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "You are right: this regression was mine. The camp guard disabled and zeroed the shared `INPUT_CONTEXT_B` after 80 ms. Rockstar uses that same input for `Leave Fire`, so pressing F made the valid prompt disappear and prevented leaving camp.\n\nI removed that broad fallback completely. The module now touches only the exact `CAMP_TEARDOWN` prompt handle and the separately remapped `INPUT_PCAMP_TEARDWN` teardown action; it never suppresses F/Context-B itself. The Lexer-Lux/Lexeditor#101 and Lexer-Lux/Lexeditor#211 checks pass, and combined build `0FBF594545C3B0D3496E1E6BB926CB541E8E2B65DE017A5F72A3C32C3C388419` is compiled and queued to install automatically when the currently running game exits. Lexer-Lux/Lexeditor#101 remains `actionable` until that install actually lands.",
